TITLE:: CommandPrompt
SUMMARY:: Text field with live command, parameter, and argument completion for an interactive command prompt.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/GuiPalette, Classes/SCViewHolder, Classes/View

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::CommandPrompt:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: providing an interactive command line with structured token chips for commands, parameters, and arguments.

As the user types:
LIST::
## In the initial state, matching LINK::Classes/Command:: names are suggested. Pressing Tab commits the command chip.
## Once a command is selected, any parameters configured in LINK::#-ambientParameters:: that match the command are automatically evaluated and bound without requiring user input or displaying a chip.
## Remaining unassigned LINK::Classes/Parameter:: names are suggested. Pressing Tab commits the parameter chip.
## When expecting an argument, the input is validated against the parameter's type and constraints (with discrete suggestions if defined). Pressing Tab commits the argument chip.
## A live validity indicator on the right indicates whether the command is incomplete (CODE::…::) or fully satisfied (CODE::✓::). Pressing Return executes the command.
## Pressing Backspace on an empty text field removes the last committed token chip and unwinds the parser state.
::

SUBSECTION:: Layout and overlay parent requirements
Because Qt clips child views to their parent bounds, suggestions cannot render outside a view's bounding box without an unmanaged overlay container. When embedding TELETYPE::CommandPrompt:: within a layout:
LIST::
## The hosting container (e.g. LINK::Classes/Window:: or root LINK::Classes/View::) must serve as the CODE::overlayParent:: without a layout assigned directly to it.
## The actual UI layout must be placed inside an inner child LINK::Classes/View:: that resizes with the container via CODE::onResize_::.
## Pass the outer unmanaged container as the CODE::overlayParent:: argument when constructing TELETYPE::CommandPrompt::. This allows the suggestions overlay to float in front of all sibling views in the Z-order without pushing or shifting sibling layout contents.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::CommandPrompt::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
Optional parent LINK::Classes/View:: or LINK::Classes/Window::. Pass CODE::nil:: when the control will be placed in a layout.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
Optional LINK::Classes/Rect:: for fixed positioning. Pass CODE::nil:: when the control will be placed in a layout. When given, its height is used for the text field and its width fixes the overall control width.

ARGUMENT:: commands
An LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/Command:: instances to match against.

ARGUMENT:: palette
An optional LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: used for styling token chips. Defaults to LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#*default::.

ARGUMENT:: ambientParameters
An optional LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: mapping parameter names to static values or getter LINK::Classes/Function::s to inject automatically when commands are committed.

ARGUMENT:: overlayParent
An optional LINK::Classes/View:: or LINK::Classes/Window:: where the suggestions overlay view will be created. Pass the root container view if the command prompt is embedded within nested layouts, or CODE::nil:: to create it on the command prompt view.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::CommandPrompt:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: ambientParameters
The ambient parameters dictionary or getter functions automatically injected into matching command parameters. Setting replaces the dictionary.

ARGUMENT:: newAmbientParameters
When setting, a LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or CODE::nil::.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event::.

METHOD:: commands
The command list used for suggestion matching. Setting replaces the list and refreshes suggestions.

ARGUMENT:: newCommands
When setting, an LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/Command:: instances.

RETURNS::
An LINK::Classes/Array:: of LINK::Classes/Command:: instances.

METHOD:: palette
The palette used for styling token chips.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette::.

METHOD:: string
The current text in the input field (not including committed chips). Setting replaces that text and refreshes suggestions.

ARGUMENT:: newString
When setting, the new input-field string.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/String::.

PRIVATE:: init, prApplySelection, prClearSuggestions, prCommitHighlightedToken, prCurrentState, prCurrentWord, prExecuteCommand, prInstallTextFieldKeyHandlers, prMakeTokenChip, prMoveSelection, prPositionSuggestionsView, prRemoveLastCommittedToken, prResetPrompt, prUpdateStatusIndicator, prUpdateSuggestions

EXAMPLES::

SUBSECTION:: Embedding CommandPrompt in a layout with an overlay parent

The example below demonstrates the simplest compliant layout setup. The outer window has no layout directly assigned, allowing the suggestions view to float above the content view.

CODE::
(
var snapCmd = Command("snap", [
	Parameter("grid", SimpleNumber, constraint: { |v| v > 0 }),
	Parameter("direction", Symbol, constraint: [\both, \left, \right])
], { |args|
	("Executing snap with grid: " ++ args[\grid] ++ ", direction: " ++ args[\direction]).postln;
});

var setCmd = Command("set", [
	Parameter("property", Symbol, constraint: [\amp, \degree, \dur, \midinote]),
	Parameter("values", Integer, isArray: true, constraint: { |v| v.inclusivelyBetween(0, 127) })
], { |args|
	("Executing set with property: " ++ args[\property] ++ ", values: " ++ args[\values]).postln;
});

var window, contentLayoutView, commandPrompt;

// 1. The root window/container serves as the overlay parent and has NO layout directly assigned.
window = Window("Command prompt layout example", Rect(100, 100, 500, 400)).front;

// 2. An inner child View hosts the UI layout and is resized to follow the window.
contentLayoutView = View(window, window.view.bounds);
window.view.onResize_({
	contentLayoutView.bounds = window.view.bounds;
});

// 3. CommandPrompt is created with overlayParent pointing to the unmanaged root window.
commandPrompt = CommandPrompt(
	parent: nil,
	bounds: nil,
	commands: [snapCmd, setCmd],
	overlayParent: window.view
);

// 4. Place CommandPrompt and other controls inside the inner content layout.
contentLayoutView.layout = VLayout(
	commandPrompt.view,
	View().background_(Color.gray(0.2)).layout_(
		VLayout(
			StaticText().string_("Main content area below").stringColor_(Color.white).align_(\center),
			StaticText().string_("Suggestions float in front without shifting this view.").stringColor_(Color.gray(0.7)).align_(\center)
		)
	)
).margins_(4).spacing_(4);
)
::
